title: The Right on the Streets
subtitle: An urgent card: the right protests against our reforms for the minorities and in the matters of the Church.
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && typeof PolishPolitics !== 'undefined' && PolishPolitics.rightCardAvailable(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card government.right_protests (Z — 1.13, decisions 1A, 2B, 3A and 4A of 8 XI 2026; P): while PPS governs and the mobilisation of
// the right is 50 or more. Concessions (half a year without such reforms), waiting (after three months on the streets the cabinet
// falls) or force. The answer costs no month; waiting brings the card back next month.
PolishPolitics.rightView(Q);
!}

= The right on the streets

[+ pl_right_text +]

- @concede
- @wait
- @force

@concede
title: Make concessions
subtitle: No new reforms for the minorities or in the matters of the Church for half a year; the crowds go home, but the minorities trust PPS less.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pl_right_result = PolishPolitics.rightChoose(Q, 'concede');
!}
go-to: result

@wait
title: Wait it out
subtitle: Clashes in the streets bring more violence, and the tension with our partners on the right grows; after three months on the streets the government falls.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pl_right_result = PolishPolitics.rightChoose(Q, 'wait');
!}
go-to: result

@force
title: Disperse the demonstrations by force
subtitle: The right withdraws, but there is more violence, democracy weakens, and the National and the Christian Democrats turn against us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pl_right_result = PolishPolitics.rightChoose(Q, 'force');
!}
go-to: result

@result
new-page: true

= The right on the streets

[+ pl_right_result +]

- @root: Continue.
